Bug report:
fix(parser): refactor parser_get_token_at to dodge souc if-arm false positive — closes final 2 cascade errors

self-hosted/parser/parser.sio:124 reliably reported "if arm type does not
match else arm" + "tail type mismatch" even in standalone compilation,
despite both arms returning the same Token type. Per project memory
(feedback_souc_line_124_diagnostic_bug), this is a souc type-comparison
bug specific to the if-expression-as-function-tail pattern when the if
arms come from different code paths (array index vs constructor call).

Workaround: split the if into an early `return` for the true branch and
let the fall-through be the function tail, dodging the if-arm type
comparison entirely.

Minimal repro that demonstrates the bug + workaround:

  // Fails: "tail type mismatch"
  fn get(idx: i64) -> Token with Panic {
      if idx >= 0 && idx < 1048576 {
          PARSER_TOKENS[idx as usize]
      } else {
          Token::with_kind(TokenKind::Eof, 0, 0, 0, 0)
      }
  }

  // Works: early return + final tail
  fn get(idx: i64) -> Token with Panic {
      if idx >= 0 && idx < 1048576 {
          return PARSER_TOKENS[idx as usize]
      }
      Token::with_kind(TokenKind::Eof, 0, 0, 0, 0)
  }

