nv2: run scheduler on all functions via basic-block chunking

Drop the machine_func_has_control_flow guard — the scheduler now
runs on every function by chopping the MIR stream into basic blocks
at LABEL / JMP / JCC / RET / CALL boundaries, scheduling each chunk
through CGPLAN_GLOBAL_BLOCK, and emitting the boundary instructions
themselves in original order. Preserves control flow + safepoint
positions; calls are treated as block boundaries so side-effecting
calls never get reordered past dependent loads.

self-host fixed-point bit-identical (md5=fd751fba…, same as the
gated-on-only-control-flow-free build); umbrella gate 12/12 PASS.

