Bug report:
[gpu] Phase Y: real GUM variance propagation in 2-comp PBPK 4-step ODE

The PTX kernel pbpk_2comp_gum_4step tracks the full 2x2 covariance
matrix (V11, V12, V22) at each Euler step via J*Sigma*J^T, with V12
held in a per-thread local register that builds from 0. Skipping V12
would underestimate V11_final ~46% at these constants, so this is the
real GUM contribution — not a diagonal-only approximation.

Gate kretikos_kaxi_phase_y_gate.sh asserts three truth claims at 10M
patients on the local A5000:
  TC-1  GPU C1_final FNV digest == CPU analytic C1_final  (bit-exact)
  TC-2  GPU V11_final FNV digest == CPU analytic V11_final (bit-exact)
  TC-3  ISO 17025 uncertainty budget CSV well-formed (u_c, u95)

Bit-exactness required mirroring the PTX op chain in the CPU oracle:
