      mb_double 4 blocks × 8 threads = 32 elements doubled
      mb_double 8 blocks × 8 threads = 64 elements doubled
  - Verified: kaxi_matrix passed=14/14 failed= on NVIDIA_L4 (job 1333)

Bug fixes:
  - kaxi_to_ptx + kaxi_to_c get_tid/get_bid/get_ntid dispatch was off-by-one:
    checked position 4 for '_' but the '_' is at position 3 in "get_tid";
    position 4 holds the discriminator letter (t/b/n). All three opcodes
    were previously emitting %tid.x. Fixed by dispatching directly on
    pos 4 letter (98=b → %ctaid.x, 110=n → %ntid.x, else → %tid.x).
    No prior pattern exercised get_bid/get_ntid so the bug was latent.

  - CI gate generalized from hardcoded 12/12 to passed=N/N for any N.

Existing gates remain green: run_kaxi_ptx.sh 8/8, run_kaxi_differential.sh 9/9.

