Bug report:
[lexer][codegen] path A: accept and decode \xHH hex string escapes

Pairs with 4481c0cc (nv2: decode \xHH in driver_append_ufn_string_literal).

Lexer: when \x is followed by two valid hex digits, advance p by 4 and
move on; otherwise fall through to the existing unknown-escape error
path (so "\xZZ" is still rejected).

Codegen: four parallel string-emit loops decode \xHH to a single byte:
  - emit_print            (x86, line ~6712)
  - compile_primary k==5  (x86 string literal expression)
  - emit_print_a64        (arm64)
  - compile_primary k==5  (arm64 string literal expression)
Each falls back to the existing legacy escape table on bad hex.

Closes the visual ANSI cluster's parity gap. Path A and N-v2 now
produce byte-identical stdout on examples/visual/05_color_demo.sio
(verified: diff <(a.elf) <(nv2.elf) exit 0).

