fix(effects): bodyless fn declarations get -1 sentinel, skip silently in codegen

Functions declared inside effect blocks (e.g. `fn pick() -> bool` inside
`effect Choice { ... }`) have no body brace. The refined body-scan now sets
FN_BODY_OPEN = -1 for these; both x86 and arm64 compilation loops skip them
with `continue` rather than erroring or miscompiling. Fixes effect_handler_basic.
Promoted gen3.elf (fixed-point 2083f689) as bin/souc-linux-x86_64.

